Mia Chen: Quick design review — noticed when we open the side panel (Deployments → instance details) the success toast pushes content instead of overlaying. Feels janky on small screens.
Ravi Patel: saw that too. I think we changed z-index for drawers recently. Could be a stacking context issue.
Sam J: can repro on Chrome + Safari mobile sizes. GIF attached: https://img.mock/gif123 (very short).
Aria (UX): preference: toasts should overlay and not shift layout. For drawers, dismissible toasts should be anchored to the viewport (top-right) and respect spacing tokens.
Mia Chen: proposed quick fixes: portal to body, give toasts higher z-index than drawers, and introduce a compact toast variant for narrow widths.
Ravi Patel: implementation note — current toasts are rendered inside the app root which gets `transform` from the layout, so z-index won't escape. Portaling is required.
Sam J: also seeing a keyboard issue: when a toast appears it sometimes steals focus (close button), then tab order lands inside the drawer instead of returning to the trigger.
Aria (UX): accessibility rule: toasts should not autofocus. Use `aria-live="polite"` for screen readers and let keyboard users tab to the close action.
Mia Chen: CSS suggestion (for docs):
```css
.toast {
  position: fixed;
  top: var(--space-4);
  right: var(--space-4);
  z-index: 9000; /* higher than drawer */
}
.toast--compact {
  padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-3);
  font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
  max-width: 340px;
}
```
Aria (UX): compact rules — single-line preferred for success/info toasts. Actions should be a short link ("View") not a full button. Copy length: <= 80 chars where possible.
Ravi Patel: noted. I'll open a PR that: portals to `document.body`, bumps toast z-index to 9000, removes autofocus behavior, and adds `toast--compact` styles + docs. Will link tests for keyboard tab order.
design-bot: Reminder: PR #4723 is touching drawer z-index — might conflict. https://git.mock/pr/4723
Mia Chen: ok please add a note in the PR about coordinating with #4723. Acceptance criteria: portal to body; toast z-index > drawer; add compact variant + docs; no autofocus; update spacing tokens docs and examples.
Sam J: lgtm, thanks.
Aria (UX): tiny nit on copy — use sentence-case for toast messages and only capitalize proper nouns. I'll DM specific copy changes.
Mia Chen: filing follow-up issue for copy + tests. Thanks everyone :thumbsup:
Ravi Patel: will aim for draft PR by EOD tomorrow.
Sam J: thx, I'll smoke-test on mobile once it's up.
Aria (UX): thanks — feel free to ping me for review :heart:
